{"Title":"An Act relative to strengthening Massachusetts’ economic leadership","BillNumber":"H5100","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":null,"Name":"Economic Development","Type":2,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2024-11-12T18:10:11.203"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"GOV7","Name":"Maura T. Healey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/GOV7","ResponseDate":"2024-03-01T10:09:50.6633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H5100/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"The committee of conference on the disagreeing votes of the two branches with reference to the Senate amendment of the House Bill relative to strengthening Massachusetts’ economic leadership (House, No. 4804), reports, in part, recommending passage of the accompanying bill (House, No. 5100).  ","DocumentText":null,"EmergencyPreamble":"Whereas, The deferred operation of this act would tend to defeat its purpose, which is to forthwith finance improvements to the commonwealth’s economic infrastructure, drive industry innovation, and promote economic opportunity and job creation, therefore it is hereby declared to be an emergency law, necessary for the immediate preservation of the public convenience.\r\n\r\n","RollCalls":[{"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Branch":"Senate","RollCallNumber":251,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Branches/Senate/RollCalls/251"},{"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Branch":"Senate","RollCallNumber":252,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Branches/Senate/RollCalls/252"}],"Attachments":[{"Description":"11A Report - Outsides","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=19655&title=11A%20Report%20-%20Outsides"},{"Description":"11A Report - Insides","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=19656&title=11A%20Report%20-%20Insides"}],"CommitteeReco